// Reference query. Not deployed in any employer environment.
// Title: MFA method registered or changed, then within 24 hours a sign-in from a country new for the user or a mail-hiding or forwarding rule (help-desk takeover chain)
// Status: untested template
// ATT&CK: T1098.005 (Account Manipulation: Device Registration), T1556.006 (Modify Authentication Process: Multi-Factor Authentication), T1564.008 (Hide Artifacts: Email Hiding Rules), T1114.003 (Email Collection: Email Forwarding Rule); ATT&CK v19.2
// Data sources: Microsoft Sentinel, AuditLogs and SigninLogs (Microsoft Entra ID data connector), OfficeActivity (Microsoft 365 data connector, Exchange operations)
// Licensing assumptions: Microsoft Sentinel workspace with the Entra ID and Microsoft 365 connectors (scenario A-17); Entra ID P1 or P2 for sign-in log access (scenario holds P2)
// Rule ID: SN-01 | Platform: Microsoft Sentinel scheduled analytics rule, run every hour, query period 14 days (see Tuning knobs) | Suggested severity: High for the full chain, Medium for two links
// Tactics: Persistence (TA0003), Credential Access (TA0006), Stealth (TA0005), Collection (TA0009)
// Answers: detection-priorities.md items 3 and 4 (Priority 1), the correlation the item 4 rationale asks for; attack-paths.md AP-2 steps 3 to 6
// Architecture context: CA-19 (security info registration control), IGA-ENTRA, RES-M365, PIP-SIEM correlation; risk register R-02
// Fictional scenario: Contoso Regional Health (fictional). Reference portfolio content.
//
// Purpose
//   AP-2 needs no malware: a help desk is talked into enrolling an attacker-controlled MFA method, then
//   the mailbox is used to divert payer or payroll payments. Any single link is noisy (people change
//   phones, travel, and file mail into folders). The chain inside 24 hours is specific, and payment
//   recovery depends on speed, so this rule runs often.
//
// Logic
//   1. AuditLogs security-info activities that Microsoft's audit activity reference lists under the
//      UserManagement category: registrations, updates to existing security info, default method changes,
//      and deletions, by the user or by an administrator. Category itself is not filtered, as in SN-02
//      and SN-07. Microsoft's token theft playbook query does filter on Category UserManagement, but the
//      Azure Monitor AuditLogs reference says Audit is the only supported value, and the activity names
//      identify the rows on their own.
//   2. SigninLogs: successful sign-ins from a country the user has not signed in from during
//      BaselineWindow (12 days), which ends where the 2-day search window (LookbackWindow) begins.
//   3. OfficeActivity: New-InboxRule, Set-InboxRule, Set-Mailbox, or UpdateInboxRules whose parameters
//      mention forwarding, redirect, delete, move, or mark-as-read settings.
//   4. Joined on the user principal name, one method change at a time: a new-country sign-in or a rule
//      counts when it falls within ChainWindow after any method change in the search window, so an
//      earlier, unrelated sign-in or rule cannot hide a later chain.
//   5. A chain is returned only in a run where one of its linked rows (the method change with its sign-in
//      or its rule) was ingested since the previous run, so a chain is reported when it completes and
//      again only when a further link arrives, such as the one that raises it to High (Tuning knobs).
//   The third AP-2 link, a banking-detail change in payer, payroll, or ERP systems, is not in Sentinel
//   under assumption A-17. Add it as a third join when those audit logs are onboarded.
//
// Known false positives
//   - New staff enrolling methods on day one, then travelling (onboarding cohorts during orientation).
//   - Affiliated physicians on travel who replace a phone and sign in abroad the same day.
//   - Users who reset methods and then create ordinary filing rules.
//
// Tuning knobs (let statements below)
//   ChainWindow, BaselineWindow   link window and the history that defines a new country.
//   MethodChangeActivities        security-info activities in scope.
//   PaymentKeywords               terms that raise severity when a rule filters on them.
//   RunInterval                   the rule's "Run query every" setting (1 hour, example value).
//   Query period: set "Lookup data from the last" to 14 days, the maximum Microsoft allows, and keep
//   BaselineWindow plus LookbackWindow within it (12 plus 2 days by default). Microsoft documents that
//   this setting is the time period the query covers, so it also bounds the baseline subquery. At a
//   shorter period the baseline is empty, the anti-join removes nothing, and every sign-in country after
//   a method change counts as new. Run the rule every RunInterval: each run reads 14 days of SigninLogs
//   for the baseline, and the 2-day LookbackWindow still completes a chain that starts near the end of
//   one run. At larger scale, a per-user country baseline maintained by a separate job (for example a
//   watchlist) can replace the baseline subquery.
//   Repeat suppression (Logic 5): an hourly run over a 2-day window would otherwise return the same chain
//   in every run until its method change ages out, and Microsoft documents that overlapping query periods
//   can cause some duplication of results. Each link keeps its ingestion_time(), and the query keeps a
//   chain only when its latest linked row was ingested within RunInterval, the ingestion_time() filter
//   that Microsoft's ingestion delay guidance uses to tie an event to one run, as SN-06 and SN-07 do.
//   Alert settings: "Trigger an alert for each event" (one alert per user chain). Map the Account entity
//   with Name and UPNSuffix from TargetAccountName and TargetUpnSuffix, a strong identifier pair in
//   Microsoft's entity reference, which notes that from July 1, 2026 the Name field holds only the UPN
//   prefix. Group alerts into one incident when all entities match, with a time frame of at least
//   LookbackWindow (2 days; Microsoft allows 5 minutes to 7 days), so a chain's first report and a later
//   upgrade share an incident. With Sentinel onboarded to the Defender portal, Microsoft documents that
//   these grouping settings take effect only when the incident is created and that the Defender
//   correlation engine may group alerts differently.
//
// Response notes
//   Disable the rule and the attacker method, revoke sessions, and require in-person or sponsor-verified
//   proofing before any new method is registered (threat-model.md section 9 item 3). Call finance and the
//   bank relationship owner at once if payment terms appear. Follow the identity compromise playbook.
//   When the account belongs to clinical staff, the clinical notification step comes before sessions are
//   revoked (clinical safety gate, ADR-008; playbook decision point D5).
//
// Validation notes
//   Not run against any workspace. Validate with a lab user in a lab tenant connected to a lab workspace:
//   register a new authenticator method, sign in from a second country through a lab egress, and create
//   a rule that moves "invoice" messages to an RSS folder. Expected telemetry: an AuditLogs row "User
//   registered security info", a SigninLogs row with the new country, and an OfficeActivity New-InboxRule
//   row. purple-team-plan.md exercise PX-09 covers the method or device registration and the method change
//   (T1098.005, T1556.006), and records a device registration that does not alert against coverage-map.md
//   section 3, item 3; PX-10 covers the hide-or-forward rule after a method change (T1564.008, T1114.003).
//   Before PX-09 and PX-10 run, record the rule's "Lookup data from the last" setting (14 days) in the
//   findings entry, and confirm that the lab user's usual country is not reported as new. Repeat
//   suppression: confirm that the chain is returned in the run after its follow-on link is ingested, not
//   again in the next hourly run, and again when a further link arrives (for example the payment rule
//   after the sign-in), with both alerts grouped into one incident.
//   Help-desk proofing itself is confirmed by tabletop.
//
// References
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/monitoring-health/reference-audit-activities
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/security/operations/token-theft-playbook
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/auditlogs
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/sentinel/scheduled-rules-overview
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/sentinel/create-analytics-rules
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/sentinel/ingestion-delay
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/sentinel/entities-reference
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/audit-log-activities
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1098/005/
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1556/006/
//
let LookbackWindow = 2d;
let ChainWindow = 24h;
// The rule's "Run query every" setting; a chain returns only when a link was ingested within it (Logic 5)
let RunInterval = 1h;
// BaselineWindow plus LookbackWindow must fit the rule's query period, at most 14 days (Tuning knobs)
let BaselineWindow = 12d;
let MethodChangeActivities = dynamic(["User registered security info", "User updated security info", "User changed default security info",
    "User deleted security info", "User registered all required security info", "Admin registered security info", "Admin updated security info",
    "Admin deleted security info"]);
let PaymentKeywords = dynamic(["invoice", "payment", "remittance", "ACH", "wire", "bank", "deposit", "payroll", "EFT"]);
// One row per security-info change; no Category filter (Logic 1)
let MethodChangeEvents =
    AuditLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookbackWindow)
    | where ActivityDisplayName in~ (MethodChangeActivities)
    | extend TargetUpn = tolower(tostring(TargetResources[0].userPrincipalName)),
             Initiator = coalesce(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName), tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName)),
             InitiatorIP = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress),
             ChangeIngested = ingestion_time()
    | where isnotempty(TargetUpn)
    | project TargetUpn, ChangeTime = TimeGenerated, ChangeIngested, ActivityDisplayName, Initiator, InitiatorIP;
// Successful sign-ins from a country absent from the user's baseline (Logic 2)
let NewCountrySignins =
    SigninLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookbackWindow)
    | where ResultType == "0"
    | extend SigninUpn = tolower(UserPrincipalName), Country = tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion), SigninIngested = ingestion_time()
    | where isnotempty(Country)
    | join kind=leftanti (
        SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated between (ago(BaselineWindow + LookbackWindow) .. ago(LookbackWindow))
        | where ResultType == "0"
        | extend SigninUpn = tolower(UserPrincipalName), Country = tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion)
        | distinct SigninUpn, Country
      ) on SigninUpn, Country
    | project SigninUpn, SigninTime = TimeGenerated, SigninIngested, Country, IPAddress;
// Rules and mailbox settings that forward, redirect, delete, move, or mark mail as read (Logic 3)
let MailRules =
    OfficeActivity
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookbackWindow)
    | where Operation in~ ("New-InboxRule", "Set-InboxRule", "Set-Mailbox", "UpdateInboxRules")
    | extend RuleUpn = tolower(UserId), RuleText = strcat(Parameters, " ", tostring(OperationProperties)), RuleIngested = ingestion_time()
    | where RuleText has_any ("ForwardTo", "ForwardAsAttachmentTo", "RedirectTo", "ForwardingSmtpAddress", "ForwardingAddress",
                              "DeleteMessage", "SoftDeleteMessage", "MoveToFolder", "MarkAsRead")
    | project RuleUpn, RuleTime = TimeGenerated, RuleIngested, RuleRecordId = OfficeId, Operation, ClientIP, PaymentRule = RuleText has_any (PaymentKeywords);
// Each follow-on signal is tested against every method change in the search window (Logic 4)
let ChainSignins =
    MethodChangeEvents
    | join kind=inner NewCountrySignins on $left.TargetUpn == $right.SigninUpn
    | where SigninTime between (ChangeTime .. (ChangeTime + ChainWindow))
    | summarize FirstNewCountrySignin = min(SigninTime), NewCountries = make_set(Country, 5), NewCountryIPs = make_set(IPAddress, 5),
        SigninLinkIngested = max(max_of(ChangeIngested, SigninIngested))
        by TargetUpn;
let ChainRules =
    MethodChangeEvents
    | join kind=inner MailRules on $left.TargetUpn == $right.RuleUpn
    | where RuleTime between (ChangeTime .. (ChangeTime + ChainWindow))
    | summarize FirstRuleTime = min(RuleTime), RuleOperations = make_set(Operation, 5), RuleClientIPs = make_set(ClientIP, 5),
        PaymentRuleCount = dcountif(RuleRecordId, PaymentRule), RuleLinkIngested = max(max_of(ChangeIngested, RuleIngested))
        by TargetUpn;
MethodChangeEvents
| summarize MethodChangeTime = min(ChangeTime), MethodChanges = make_set(ActivityDisplayName, 5),
    Initiators = make_set(Initiator, 5), InitiatorIPs = make_set(InitiatorIP, 5)
    by TargetUpn
| join kind=leftouter ChainSignins on TargetUpn
| join kind=leftouter ChainRules on TargetUpn
| extend SigninAfterChange = isnotnull(FirstNewCountrySignin),
         RuleAfterChange = isnotnull(FirstRuleTime)
| where SigninAfterChange or RuleAfterChange
// Return the chain only in a run where one of its linked rows was newly ingested (Logic 5)
| extend LatestLinkIngested = max_of(coalesce(SigninLinkIngested, RuleLinkIngested), coalesce(RuleLinkIngested, SigninLinkIngested))
| where LatestLinkIngested > ago(RunInterval)
| extend SuggestedSeverity = case(
    SigninAfterChange and RuleAfterChange, "High: method change, new-country sign-in, and a mail-hiding or forwarding rule",
    RuleAfterChange and coalesce(PaymentRuleCount, 0) > 0, "High: method change, then a rule touching payment-related mail",
    "Medium: method change followed by one follow-on signal")
| extend TimeGenerated = max_of(MethodChangeTime, coalesce(FirstNewCountrySignin, MethodChangeTime), coalesce(FirstRuleTime, MethodChangeTime)),
         TargetAccountName = tostring(split(TargetUpn, "@")[0]),
         TargetUpnSuffix = tostring(split(TargetUpn, "@")[1])
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUpn, TargetAccountName, TargetUpnSuffix, SuggestedSeverity, MethodChangeTime, MethodChanges, Initiators, InitiatorIPs,
    FirstNewCountrySignin, NewCountries, NewCountryIPs, FirstRuleTime, RuleOperations, RuleClientIPs, PaymentRuleCount, LatestLinkIngested
